  "limitations": [
    "No canonical bootstrap compatibility binding, format freeze, production entrypoint, or persisted limit-envelope certification.",
    "Existing singleton membership checks and leader wait are reused; no certification of exact singleton or joint/foreign recovered membership.",
    "Closed-member admission recovery still uses the existing separate path and is not qualified here.",
    "No production clock, worker materialization, namespace generation continuity, fencing, or complete cutover claim.",
    "Only the new factory entrypoint owns preparation after first poll; ambient constructors retain their previous cancellation behavior.",
    "The caller accepting a Singleton remains responsible for explicit shutdown. No Singleton Drop implementation is added.",
    "Factory custody depends on its trusted backend contract; the descriptor backend supplies the qualified concrete implementation.",
    "Never-polled futures, panics, process death, runtime destruction and exhaustive scheduling are outside these cancellation witnesses.",
    "Two selected compiled faults are not a general mutation score. No new syscall-injection or power-loss qualification is claimed."
  ],
  "new_witnesses": [
    "Binding node/epoch/namespace and invalid limits refuse before a counted factory invocation.",
    "Successful constructor handoff commits AdvanceTime(17) and reads it through real Raft.",
    "Canceled receiver during a private per-construction gate after Raft::new explicitly stops Raft after the gate releases, even with another Raft handle alive.",
    "A result received without the private handoff acknowledgment explicitly stops Raft while the received Singleton remains alive. Public receive/ack/return has no intervening await.",
    "Descriptor create/write/read/shutdown/reopen after root rename preserves the ambient replacement and retains all four actual directory locks.",
    "Caller cancellation during held factory and held parent sync retains all four locks, then releases custody after owned startup/shutdown; initialized Singleton reopen succeeds.",
    "Existing metadata-only journal is refused by Singleton reopen rather than adopted as new membership."
  ],
